    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         ORBIT DESKTOP — window-chrome palette
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         The desktop client is modelled as a WINDOW: a command bar at the top,
         one or more panes in the middle, a status strip along the bottom.
         Each of those is a distinct surface, and the ladder runs:

             od_window   deepest  — the frame behind everything
             od_pane     base     — a content region
             od_pane_raised +     — the selected / focused region
             od_well     recessed — an inset field INSIDE a pane

         A well is darker than its parent; a panel is lighter. That single rule
         is what makes the layout read as depth instead of as stacked boxes.

         Accent discipline: ember marks SELECTED, PRIMARY ACTION or LIVE.
         Nothing decorative is ever ember.
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

